                <pb facs="ec_d12-1" n="1" xml:id="ec_d12-1"/>

                <head>EC–12. Editorial Note</head>
                <p>Ambassador Christian M. Ravndal and Minister of Foreign Affairs Carlos Tobar
                    Zaldumbide exchanged notes at Quito on January 20 and February 11, 1960,
                    constituting an agreement for a five-year loan of two <pb facs="0633" n="545"
                        type="typeset" xml:id="pg545"/> United States patrol craft (escort vessels)
                    to Ecuador. For the text of the agreement, see 11 UST 241.</p>
                <p>On February 24, 1960, at Quito, Ambassador Ravndal and Foreign Minister Tobar
                    signed an Agreement Relating to a Cooperative Program in Ecuador for the
                    Observation and Tracking of Satellites and Space Vehicles. It provided for
                    continuing the operation and maintenance of the satellite tracking station at
                    Paramo de Cotopaxi, known as the Quito Tracking Station Facility. For the text
                    of the agreement, see 11 UST 179.</p>
            </div>
